From: Hoang Viet Pham <hoang.pham@adtran.com>
Date: Wed, 01 Apr 2026 08:20:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: fix TX completion handling for offloaded flows

The transmit completion of a frame of an offloaded flow can find an
skb without a device, and the queue lookup then reads a NULL
pointer. The completion now skips the queue accounting for such an
skb.

Signed-off-by: Hoang Viet Pham <hoang.pham@adtran.com>
---

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -1262,10 +1262,12 @@ static int airoha_qdma_tx_napi_poll(stru
 		q->queued--;
 
 		if (skb) {
-			struct netdev_queue *txq;
+			if (skb->dev) {
+				struct netdev_queue *txq;
 
-			txq = skb_get_tx_queue(skb->dev, skb);
-			netdev_tx_completed_queue(txq, 1, skb->len);
+				txq = skb_get_tx_queue(skb->dev, skb);
+				netdev_tx_completed_queue(txq, 1, skb->len);
+			}
 			dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
 		}
 
